WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.959
Hey, David, is the idea of impeaching Trump
over?

00:00:03.959 --> 00:00:09.080
I'm not hearing very much about it, but at
the same time, supposedly Jerry Nadler is

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.510
running an impeachment inquiry.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.850
What the Hell is going on?

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.660
So listen, here's the answer.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:14.770
I don't care either way.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.550
And what I mean by that is we should know
if there's going to be an impeachment inquiry

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.550
or not.

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:25.710
But I've said before, at this point, the possibility
of the impeachment inquiry is doing nothing

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.710
for the left.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:27.710
It's a distraction.

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.710
Okay?

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.800
If anything, it's hurting the left internal
debates about should we do an impeachment

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.690
inquiry or should we not do an impeachment
inquiry?

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.339
Pelosi says no, and Nadler says yes, or whoever
says yes, no, whatever.

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:42.170
And they get into these arguments.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.390
That's how you lose.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:44.390
Okay?

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.820
Option one, start the impeachment inquiry.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:47.820
Right away.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:48.820
I'm fine with that.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.360
I think that that would be damaging to Donald
Trump.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:56.100
It would take away some of the power of Donald
Trump's narrative setting a ability within

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.100
the media.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.100
That would be fine.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:03.620
Decide we're going to table the impeachment
inquiry until, for example, November 1st,

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:10.509
2019 or February 1st, 2020 or whenever Democrats
say this is when the impeachment inquiry will

00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:12.259
be most damaging to Donald Trump.

00:01:12.259 --> 00:01:13.259
Great.

00:01:13.259 --> 00:01:14.259
I'm fine with that as well.

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:15.990
Yes, it's playing politics.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.819
Oh No, it's okay.

00:01:18.819 --> 00:01:23.729
If that's the idea that we could do more damage
to Trump by starting the impeachment inquiry

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:25.700
at some later point, let's do it.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.880
Or no impeachment inquiry, let's just win
2020 and put our efforts on that.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:34.579
I'm fine with that as well, so I don't know
if the idea of impeaching Trump is over or

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:38.469
more accurately doing the impeachment inquiry,
which would be the first step.

00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:41.499
The the, the sort of pre impeachment inquiry.

00:01:41.499 --> 00:01:48.090
I don't really care as long as everybody is
on the same page and we understand what the

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.909
impeachment inquiry would lead to and what
it would not lead to.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:56.529
The impeachment inquiry would lead to making
public a lot of the content of the Mueller

00:01:56.529 --> 00:01:58.319
report, which most people haven't read.

00:01:58.319 --> 00:01:59.319
That's good.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.319
It will damage Trump.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:03.950
It will lead to media stories about the impeachment
inquiry.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:04.950
That's good.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:10.299
That's time that is not being manipulated
by Donald Trump and other good things.

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:15.940
The impeachment inquiry will not lead to the
removal of Donald Trump via an impeachment

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.560
conviction in the Senate.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.560
It just won't.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:22.630
Okay, so as long as we understand what it
will and won't do, I'm fine with doing it

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:27.019
now, doing it in six months or doing it, not
at all, but we've got to stop going back and

00:02:27.019 --> 00:02:28.019
forth about it.

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:30.720
And in that sense, I'm not displeased.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.569
That discussions of impeachment has sort of
evaporated.

00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:38.290
Meanwhile, though, based on Trump's erratic
behavior over the last 10 days or so since

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:43.970
we started and since ended our show vacation,
more and more discussions of removal under

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:49.250
the 25th Amendment for being unfit to serve
have surfaced and are perpetuating themselves

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.750
and social media also don't know that that's
going to go anywhere, but I'm totally fine

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:58.719
with uh, not pursuing impeachment against
Donald Trump and I'm completely fine with

00:02:58.719 --> 00:02:58.930
doing it as well.

